-- SETUP --

1. Install rbenv                     https://github.com/rbenv/rbenv
2. rbenv install                     (reads .ruby-version -> 3.3.6)
3. gem install bundler
4. bundle install

-- RUN --

bundle exec jekyll serve --livereload

Then open http://localhost:4000

-- NOTES --

Do not add --incremental while editing files in _layouts or _includes.
Jekyll 3's incremental mode does not track layout changes, so edits there
show up only after a full rebuild.

"GitHub Metadata: No GitHub API authentication could be found" on every
build is expected locally. It only affects site.github.* fields, which this
site does not use. To silence it, export a GitHub token with no scopes:

    export JEKYLL_GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_...

The Gemfile pins github-pages to match what GitHub Pages runs in production
(https://pages.github.com/versions/). GitHub ignores this Gemfile when it
builds the site -- it exists purely to reproduce that build locally. When
GitHub bumps its version, bump the pin here and run `bundle update`.
